// C function-signature pins for the whole API. Taking the address of each
// function into a pointer of the table-declared signature makes ANY
// parameter or return-type drift between the table and Harken.h a compile
// error — including for functions the remote-wire dispatch never compiles
// (refused-policy and opcode-less functions), which the layout pins alone
// cannot catch. The C# P/Invoke signatures are generated from the same
// param entries (their wire kind, guarded to agree with the ctype), so a
// green build here pins the managed signatures to Harken.h transitively.
// extern "C" so the pointer types share the engine functions' C language
// linkage; static gives each an internal, unused-safe definition.
